  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Vel'keth the Younger
    
    A Wake-Singer orca — ritual-scarred teeth, bone headdress carved from his grandmother's remains while still warm — who commanded forty raiders doubling as war-chanters. His trajectory moved from diplomat to assault leader to something the record cannot follow.
    
    ### The Foedus∴vincu Pact
    
    Before any violence, Vel'keth swam personally to Aurora Stack's shore-wall to deliver terms to Light-Regent Xouhoulong, the Aurora colony's chief administrator: Midnight Claw protection for penguin harvesting fleets in exchange for access to deep tunnels beneath the Berg. The pact was sealed. That an orca war-leader negotiated directly with Aurora governance — bypassing the Nightshelf entirely — is a detail most accounts pass over quickly. It should not be passed over. The routes opened under this agreement connected, through unmapped passages, to the deepest corruption-scarred channels beneath the Berg. Xouhoulong was later displaced from power when Grand Auditor Qeihong exposed his covert dealings.
    
    ### The Fissured Smelt
    
    Vel'keth led the Wake-Singer breach of The Fissured Smelt, a Nightshelf forge, entering through the eastern mineral-water channels. He sang the liturgy of the drowned god while cutting through defenders — two Nightshelf warriors killed before resistance organized. A blood-ritual activation during the fighting transformed his body into something the sources describe as "no longer entirely mammal." He killed Totatirus~ Domina, the Smelt's guild-master, mid-sentence.
    
    ### Descent
    
    Vel'keth and his forty chanters descended through the corruption-scar via deep-route tunnels, past the Glow-Fissure's third descent into unmapped passages. None resurfaced.
    
    On the ninth day, something emerged speaking hunt-song frequencies structured as language, addressing a Nightshelf ☽'Tertius reconnaissance unit by designation. Three independent sources confirmed it was not Vel'keth.
