  annotation "note_1771592407570_1", anchor: "He killed Totatirus~ Domina, the Smelt's guild-master, mid-sentence", text: "The sources record Vel'keth's liturgy in full. Four stanzas. Rhythmic structure annotated. They do not record what Domina was saying when she died. Not a syllable.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771592407570_2", anchor: "Three independent sources confirmed it was not Vel'keth", text: "Three sources independently confirmed what it *wasn't*. None ventured what it was. This is the investigative equivalent of establishing that the fire is not a fish, then closing the case. More to the point: it addressed a Nightshelf reconnaissance unit *by designation*. Designations are coded. Nightshelf designations are coded *twice*. Whatever came back up knew things Vel'keth could not have known going down. The interesting question was never 'was it Vel'keth.'", type: :skepticism, display: :full
